with minimal moisture exposure. Reconstituted: 2-8 deg C, use within about 30 days, and avoid freeze-thaw cycles."}]}]]}]],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"children":"COA"}],["$","dd",null,{"children":["$","$Lc",null,{"href":"/pt/coa/cgl10/","target":"_blank","children":"Ver certificado"}]}]]}]]}]]}]
39:["$","aside",null,{"className":"purchase-column","aria-label":"Opções de compra","children":["$","$L3d",null,{"specification":"10mg x 10 vials /box"}]}]
3a:["$","section",null,{"className":"detail-longform","aria-label":"Product details","children":[["$","$L3e",null,{"tabs":[{"id":"overview","label":"Overview"},{"id":"research","label":"Research"},{"id":"dosing","label":"Dosing & Protocol"},{"id":"sideeffects","label":"Side Effects"},{"id":"reviews","label":"Avaliações - 775"},{"id":"qa","label":"Perguntas - 0"}]}],[["$","article","overview",{"id":"overview","className":"content-panel","children":[false,["$","div",null,{"className":"panel-body","children":[["$","$4","0",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"What is CGL10?"}],null,[["$","p","0",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Cagrilintide is a long‑acting acylated analogue of the pancreatic hormone amylin, designed for once‑weekly subcutaneous administration. It activates central amylin receptors to promote satiety, slow gastric emptying, and reduce food intake. In phase 2 and phase 3 trials, cagrilintide produced dose‑dependent weight loss with a predominantly gastrointestinal side‑effect profile"}]}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","$4","1",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Research context"}],null,[["$","p","0",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Cagrilintide is an acylated, long‑acting analogue of amylin—a hormone co‑secreted with insulin from pancreatic beta cells[2][7]. Native amylin promotes satiation, slows gastric emptying, and inhibits postprandial glucagon secretion[8][9]. By acting on central amylin receptors (particularly in the area postrema and hindbrain), cagrilintide reduces appetite and energy intake. Lipid modifications extend its half‑life to approximately 160–195 hours, enabling once‑weekly dosing"}]}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}],["$","article","research",{"id":"research","className":"content-panel","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-title","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Research"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"panel-body","children":[["$","$4","0",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Reference literature focus"}],null,[["$","p","0",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Cagrilintide is dosed at 600 mcg–4.5 mg weekly by subcutaneous injection in educational protocols, starting low and titrating upward. A 10 mg vial reconstituted with bacteriostatic water yields about 3.33 mg/mL. This information is for research and educational use only."}]}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}],["$","article","dosing",{"id":"dosing","className":"content-panel","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-title","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Dosing & Protocol"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"panel-body","children":[["$","$4","0",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"LPPeptide handling reference"}],null,[["$","p","0",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Reconstitute: Add 3.0 mL bacteriostatic water → ~3.33 mg/mL concentration.\nTypical weekly range: 0.6–4.5 mg once weekly (gradual titration over 4–6 weeks).\nEasy measuring: At 3.33 mg/mL, 1 unit = 0.01 mL ≈ 0.0333 mg (33.3 mcg) on a U‑100 insulin syringe.\nStorage: Lyophilized: store frozen at −20 °C (−4 °F); after reconstitution, refrigerate at 2–8 °C (35.6–46.4 °F) and use within 30 days."}]}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","$4","1",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Preparation"}],null,[["$","p","0",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Draw 3.0 mL bacteriostatic water with a sterile syringe.\nInject slowly down the vial wall; avoid foaming or vigorous agitation.\nGently swirl or roll until fully dissolved (do not shake).\nLabel with date and concentration; refrigerate at 2–8 °C (35.6–46.4 °F), protected from light.\nUse within 30 days of reconstitution; discard if cloudy or particulate matter appears."}]}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","$4","2",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Storage"}],null,[["$","p","0",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Proper storage preserves peptide integrity and potency.\nLyophilized: Store at −20 °C (−4 °F) in dry, dark conditions; minimize moisture exposure.\nReconstituted: Refrigerate at 2–8 °C (35.6–46.4 °F); use within 30 days and avoid freeze–thaw cycles.\nAllow vials to reach room temperature before opening to reduce condensation uptake"}]}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}],"$L3f"],"$L40","$L41",[],"$L42","$L43"]}]
