3f:["$","article","sideeffects",{"id":"sideeffects","className":"content-panel","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-title","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Side Effects"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"panel-body","children":[["$","$4","0",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Safety observations"}],null,[["$","p","0",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Complementary strategies for optimal outcomes.\nPair with a balanced, protein‑forward diet tailored to individual energy needs.\nCombine resistance training and aerobic activity to support metabolic health and preserve lean mass.\nPrioritize adequate sleep (7–9 hours) and stress management for adherence and recovery.\nMonitor hydration and electrolytes, especially if experiencing gastrointestinal side effects"}]}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","$4","1",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Contraindications"}],null,[["$","p","0",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Weight reduction: In the phase 2 trial, cagrilintide 4.5 mg weekly produced approximately 10.8% body weight loss over 26 weeks versus 3.0% with placebo.\nCombination therapy: When combined with semaglutide 2.4 mg (CagriSema), phase 3 REDEFINE trials showed approximately 20% weight loss at 68 weeks, exceeding results with either agent alone.\nDose‑dependent efficacy: Higher doses (2.4–4.5 mg) demonstrate greater weight loss than lower doses (0.3–1.2 mg).\nSide effects: Primarily gastrointestinal—nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, and constipation—which are generally mild‑to‑moderate and transient. Gradual titration helps minimize these effects.\nInjection‑site reactions: Occasional mild redness or irritation at subcutaneous injection sites"}]}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}]
